<!--
We can use type selectors to target specific elements in your HTML and apply custom styles. In the <style> tag, add CSS declaration so h1 becomes blue and p becomes red.

The property for setting the color of the text is color.

h1 should have color blue

p should have color red
-->

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Hello World</title>
  <style>
    h1 {
      color:blue;
    }
    p {
      color:red;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Make this heading blue.</h1>
  <p>Make this paragraph red.</p>
</body>
</html>